derived.json schema \"mailing_activity_bounces\" has x-primary-key=null and required=null; a corpus-wide scan for any bounce row identity token (bounce_id, bounces_id, \"bounce id\", \"Unique bounce\", activity_id, row_id, record_id) returns 0 hits across all 212 articles. The prior R7 \"dimensional grain\" key was INFERRED, not sourced — its own evidence string conceded \"not a vendor-declared identity\" — and it caused a CONFIRMED runtime failure (HybridE2E: 53 of 248 rows failed, \"no rows returned from SQL\", because the always-empty PK part user_id never reaches the INSERT parameter list). It is removed as a fabrication. Deferred to runtime D4: InformzConnector.BuildRecord already falls back to computeContentHash(raw) over the full row when no PK is declared, so the grid stays syncable and dedupable keyless, and DiscoverFieldsViaFetch/pickKeyFromStats may promote a data-proven soft key once a live sample exists. All 9 fields are IsReadOnly and the object is non-writable, so the Postgres keyless-save failure mode cannot arise.",
